APPENDIX N — COUNT REGENERATION SPECIFICATION

Principle 19.1: all manuscript counts are generated from master files, not typed. The script (regen.py) also enforces the calculus (Principle 19.3).

```
INPUT: claims.csv, sources.csv, links.json

# Unique claims
claims_unique = COUNT(DISTINCT claim_id IN claims.csv)

# Unique sources
sources_unique = COUNT(DISTINCT source_id IN sources.csv)

# Unique lineages
lineages_unique = COUNT(DISTINCT lineage IN sources.csv)

# Claim–source links
links_total = COUNT(links IN links.json)
links_supporting  = COUNT(links WHERE relationship == "supports")
links_contextual  = COUNT(links WHERE relationship == "contextualizes")
links_contradict  = COUNT(links WHERE relationship == "contradicts")
links_duplicate   = COUNT(links WHERE relationship == "duplicate-archive")

# k per claim (per component where declared)
FOR each claim c:
    FOR each component g IN c.declared_components (or [c] if none):
        k[c,g] = COUNT(DISTINCT lineage
                       FOR link IN links WHERE link.claim_id == c
                       AND link.component == g
                       AND link.relationship == "supports"
                       AND link.R >= 2)
    k[c] = MAX(k[c,g] over g)   # total independent lineages across components
    k_eff[c] = MIN(k[c,g] over g)  # weakest essential component

# Cap
FOR each claim c:
    C_max[c] = 1 IF k_eff[c] == 0 ELSE 2 IF k_eff[c] == 1 ELSE 4

# Enforce raw-cap separation
FOR each claim c:
    assert CC[c] == MIN(CC_raw[c], C_max[c])
    assert AC[c] == MIN(AC_raw[c], C_max[c])

# Enforce AC ≤ 2 while DT untested
FOR each claim c:
    assert NOT (c.disconfirming_status == "untested" AND AC[c] > 2)

# Enforce AC_country
FOR each claim c:
    IF NOT c.country_applicable:
        AC_country[c] = NA
    ELIF c.state_act:
        AC_country[c] = AC[c]
    ELIF c.international_dependencies_test_status == "tested":
        AC_country[c] = AC[c]
    ELSE:
        AC_country[c] = MAX(1, AC[c] - 1)   # DTU label if AC > 1

# Enforce no stored score above cap
FOR each claim c:
    assert CC[c] <= C_max[c]
    assert AC[c] <= C_max[c]
    assert NOT (c.k_eff == 0 AND (CC[c] > 1 OR AC[c] > 1))

# Referential integrity
FOR each link IN links:
    assert link.claim_id IN claims.csv
    assert link.source_id IN sources.csv

# Audit completeness
FOR each claim c:
    ac_complete[c] = ALL(AC_checklist[c])

# Output
PRINT claims_unique, sources_unique, lineages_unique,
      links_total, links_supporting, links_contextual,
      links_contradict, links_duplicate
PRINT dashboard table (claim, k, k_eff, C_max, CC_raw, CC,
                       AC_raw, AC, AC_country, IE, status)
PRINT claims with ac_complete == FALSE (research tasks)
PRINT previous-version scores beside current (source of Appendix J change list)
```

Rule N.1. Any manuscript statement of a count must cite script output.

Rule N.2. On split, merge, or add, re-run script; record delta in revision log.

Rule N.3. The dashboard of Appendix A is the script output, not a manually assembled table.

Rule N.4 (new). The script enforces the calculus: it exits with an error if (i) any stored score exceeds its cap; (ii) any AC exceeds 2 while its disconfirming test is untested; (iii) any unsourced claim carries a score above 1; (iv) a link names a claim or source that does not exist.

