APPENDIX P — GLOSSARY

Term Definition
Claim A bounded falsifiable proposition about a specific contribution, event, relationship, or outcome (§6.2).
Declared components Dated events bundled inside a single claim, each evaluated separately; effective support is that of the weakest component (§6.4).
Layer A–H The eight analytical contribution layers (§6.1).
Lineage The chain of origin and reuse; sources in one lineage are not independent (§7.2).
CC_raw Chronology raw score (what the type of evidence would support) (§8.1).
AC_raw Attribution raw score (§8.1).
CC / AC Final scores = min(raw, C_max) (§8.2).
IE Impact evidence 0–4; descriptive type, not quality (§8.1, §11.1).
MQ Methodological quality of outcome evidence, 1–4 (§11.2).
POP Population specification (§11.2).
DIST Distributional profile (§11.2).
CU Causal uncertainty statement (§11.2).
k Distinct supporting lineages with R ≥ 2, computed per component (§8.1, App. E).
k_eff Minimum of k over the claim's components (§8.1).
C_max(k_eff) Single operative independence cap: 1 if k_eff=0; 2 if k_eff=1; 4 if k_eff≥2 (§8.2).
AC_country Country-attribution value: max(1, AC−1) when dependency untested; =AC under state-act or tested dependency; NA for non-US claims (§8.4).
State-act exemption AC_country = AC when the actor is the government and the proposition is its own act (§8.4).
Indeterminate (Ind.) k_eff = 0, or CC/AC = 1 — absence of support, not weak support (§8.3 R5).
DTU (dependency-untested) AC_country = 1 by §8.4 rule while AC > 1 — country step untested (§8.4).
"Not established" Current record does not justify a date/conclusion; research task (§7.3).
"Not applicable" Field genuinely does not apply (§7.3).
E1–E5 Category, evidence, attribution, impact, and synthesis collapse (§2).
AC-1…AC-13 Audit-completion criteria (§25).
R, P, I, L, D Probative profile dimensions: direct relevance, archival proximity, institutional interest, locator precision, independence group (§9.1).
Reproduction Reviewer-with-packet re-derivation within one band (§12.1).
Pre-registration Public deposit of hypotheses, claims, and analysis plan before review (§12.5; App. O).
Synthesis claim Causal meta-claim that must be decomposed into ≥ 3 components before IE > 1 (§9.5).

